Affected component: OSPF default route origination from the WAN router (r1). Mechanism: The internal L3 gateways (DSWs/CSWs) have no 0.0.0.0/0 in their OSPF RIBs, so when hosts try to reach an Internet address they send to their gateway, which immediately returns “Destination Net Unreachable.” Evidence: pc1 -> 203.0.113.1 is rejected by 10.1.0.2 (gateway). FRR route tables on csw1/csw2/dswa1/dswa2/dswb1/dswb2 show no default route. On r1, FRR is configured with “default-information originate,” but r1’s kernel routing table has no default route at all; therefore, FRR does not actually inject a default (it advertises none: external LSA count 0). Localization: r1 (Linux kernel routing table and FRR OSPF on r1). Root cause: 
