[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: OSPF default route origination from the WAN router (r1). Mechanism: The internal L3 gateways (DSWs/CSWs) have no 0.0.0.0/0 in their OSPF RIBs, so when hosts try to reach an Internet address they send to their gateway, which immediately returns “Destination Net Unreachable.” Evidence: pc1 -> 203.0.113.1 is rejected by 10.1.0.2 (gateway). FRR route tables on csw1/csw2/dswa1/dswa2/dswb1/dswb2 show no default route. On r1, FRR is configured with “default-information originate,” but r1’s kernel routing table has no default route at all; therefore, FRR does not actually inject a default (it advertises none: external LSA count 0). Localization: r1 (Linux kernel routing table and FRR OSPF on r1). Root cause: Missing kernel default route on r1 prevents OSPF from originating a default, leaving the entire campus without an Internet route. Corrective fix: Install a default route on r1 to the ISP next-hops and let FRR advertise it. Example (Linux): ip route add default nexthop via 203.0.113.1 dev eth2 weight 1 nexthop via 203.0.113.5 dev eth3 weight 1. Alternatively, add equivalent static(s) in FRR (zebra) and keep “default-information originate” (or use “default-information originate always” if you must advertise even when the default is momentarily absent). After this, DSWs/CSWs will learn 0/0 and hosts will reach the Internet. Note: r1 can reach both ISP peers now (203.0.113.1/203.0.113.5), confirming physical/peer links are up. 
=== END ===